---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../components/studio.css";
---

<Layout title="Good to know — Studio" wordmark="admin">
  <main class="admin" id="main">
    <section id="sec-info" class="prose">
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
      <p>
        When a buyer taps “Send inquiry” on a painting page, their note lands
        straight in your inbox — hit reply and it goes to them. Send it from
        your author@barbart.ca email address. After shipping, open the piece and
        mark it sold.
      </p>
      <h3>Taking the photo</h3>
      <p>
        Daylight beats ceiling light: hang the painting near a window and
        photograph it straight on, filling the frame. That one photo also builds
        the “try it on your wall” preview, so a blurry upload means a blurry
        preview.
      </p>
      <h3>After you press Publish</h3>
      <p>
        The page goes live within a few minutes — the site rebuilds itself after
        every save. A draft with a “Publish on” date goes live by itself once
        that day comes; just open the studio and it happens.
      </p>
      <h3>If a painting disappears</h3>
      <p>
        It is almost certainly a draft or in the trash, not gone. Deleted
        paintings rest in the Trash fold for 30 days and restore in one tap;
        drafts sit under Available until published.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://chitchats.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Chit Chats</a
          > — cheapest tracked Canada/US shipping.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.pirateship.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >Pirate Ship</a
          > — backup for US labels.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Getting paid: start with e-transfer. When a buyer writes back, send them
        your e-transfer address and hold the painting until the money lands — we
        can set up a checkout thing later if we want.
      </p>
      <details>
        <summary>Advanced Settings</summary>
        <p class="hint">
          Email alerts <span id="flag-email">…</span> · iOS push <span
            id="flag-push">…</span
          > · auto-post <span id="flag-social">…</span>
        </p>
        <label
          >Local API token (only needed on this device if Access is off)
          <input id="admin-token" type="password" autocomplete="off" />
        </label>
        <p class="hint">
          This browser can keep working offline: <span id="cap-sw">…</span> · sending
          in the background: <span id="cap-sync">…</span> · network: <span
            id="cap-net">…</span
          >
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script src="../../components/AdminPanel.ts"></script>

<style>
  #sec-info ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  /* Advanced drawer eases open where the browser allows it; elsewhere it
     simply appears, as before. */
  #sec-info details {
    interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
  }
  #sec-info details::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    transition:
      block-size 0.35s ease,
      content-visibility 0.35s ease;
    /* !important: the transition shorthand below resets behavior to
       normal, and the minifier sorts this declaration first — without
       it the unfold silently snaps. */
    transition-behavior: allow-discrete !important;
  }
  #sec-info details[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
  }
  /* The settings themselves fade in a beat behind the unfold, so the
     words arrive once their room exists instead of squeezing through
     mid-animation. Opacity-only, so it still runs under reduced motion.
     The display step rides along discretely with a @starting-style:
     without it the freshly rendered content has no starting opacity
     and pops in on some runs. */
  #sec-info details > :not(summary) {
    opacity: 0;
    transition:
      opacity 0.25s ease 0.08s,
      display 0.33s ease;
    /* Important: the shorthand resets behavior to normal, and the
       minifier sorts this declaration first — without it the display
       step snaps and the fade only sometimes plays. */
    transition-behavior: allow-discrete !important;
  }
  #sec-info details[open] > :not(summary) {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  @starting-style {
    #sec-info details[open] > :not(summary) {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #sec-info details::details-content {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
